%% ============================================================================
%% Diagram 7 - Failure recovery (EC2 instance failure)
%% Purpose: what happens when an EC2 instance dies - self healing
%% ============================================================================
sequenceDiagram
    participant ALB as ALB
    participant EC1 as EC2 App AZ-a
    participant EC2 as EC2 App AZ-b
    participant ASG as Auto Scaling Group
    participant LT as Launch Template
    participant D as Docker stack
    participant S as SSM / Secrets Manager

    Note over EC1: Instance fails (health check timeout)
    ALB->>ALB: health check fails on EC1
    ALB-->>ASG: instance marked UNHEALTHY
    ASG-->>ALB: keeps traffic on EC2 (AZ-b)
    ASG->>ASG: detects unhealthy instance
    ASG->>LT: launches replacement instance
    LT->>D: user-data runs: install docker, ECR login
    D->>S: read image params (SSM) + DB secret
    D->>D: compose up (retries until healthy)
    ALB->>D: health check /health returns 200
    ALB-->>ASG: new instance HEALTHY
    Note over ASG: capacity restored - no manual intervention